---
import { site } from "../config/site";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy notice | CareMin"
  description="CareMin marketing website privacy notice."
  noindex={true}
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container page-hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p>How information submitted through the CareMin marketing website is handled.</p>
      <div class="review-notice" role="note">
        <strong>Pre-launch placeholder:</strong> This notice requires review by an Australian privacy
        professional and confirmation of the operating legal entity before publication.
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 5 August 2026</p>

      <h2>Scope</h2>
      <p>
        This draft notice applies to the public CareMin marketing website. It does not cover the
        separate CareMin application or provider data stored in that product.
      </p>

      <h2>Information collected</h2>
      <p>
        If you request a walkthrough, the form asks for your name, work email, organisation, number
        of homes, message, and consent to be contacted. Do not submit resident names, health
        information, payroll data, or other sensitive operational information through this website.
      </p>

      <h2>How enquiry information is used</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiry information is used to understand and respond to your request, arrange a product
        walkthrough, and keep a record of the conversation. It is not used to create a CareMin
        product account automatically.
      </p>

      <h2>Form delivery</h2>
      <p>
        The enquiry form uses FormSubmit to deliver the submitted fields to the CareMin contact
        email. This means the form provider processes the information on CareMin's behalf. Its
        documentation states that submissions may be retained in a submission archive for 30 days.
        This arrangement must be confirmed as part of the legal review before launch.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Analytics are disabled by default. Privacy-friendly analytics may be enabled later through
        the site's public configuration. This notice must be updated before that occurs.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy questions, email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a
        >. The legal entity name and any required Australian contact details will be added after
        legal review.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
